From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:27:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Enable the GPADC

The board wires the GPADC channels 0 to 4 to fixed resistor dividers
from the 1.8 V AVCC rail, which carry boot strap and board ID levels
(schematic V1.10, sheet 06): BOOT-SEL (505 mV), DDR-PARA-SEL (608 mV),
BOARD-ID-SEL (1315 mV), USB-UPGRADE-COMBO1-SEL (1315 mV) and BOARD-ID
(576 mV). Channels 5 and 6 are not connected. Enable the node with a
child for each wired channel.

The LRADC input has only a pull-up resistor and no key, so the LRADC
node stays disabled.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: channels 0 to 4 read the divider voltages
given above.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts   | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 2339be766504..69c077594490 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -274,6 +274,34 @@ ext_rgmii_phy: ethernet-phy@1 {
 	};
 };
 
+&gpadc {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * Fixed resistor dividers from AVCC (1.8 V), read as straps and
+	 * board IDs by the boot chain. Channels 5 and 6 are not connected.
+	 */
+	channel@0 {
+		reg = <0>;	/* BOOT-SEL, 505 mV */
+	};
+
+	channel@1 {
+		reg = <1>;	/* DDR-PARA-SEL, 608 mV */
+	};
+
+	channel@2 {
+		reg = <2>;	/* BOARD-ID-SEL, 1315 mV */
+	};
+
+	channel@3 {
+		reg = <3>;	/* USB-UPGRADE-COMBO1-SEL, 1315 mV */
+	};
+
+	channel@4 {
+		reg = <4>;	/* BOARD-ID, 576 mV */
+	};
+};
+
 &gpu {
 	/*
 	 * Fixed operating point from the OPP table: the driver sets VDD-GPU
